Z||000001||DXR_DAD||04-30-2000||10:18 PM||||Cliff's car is the GT/Aero fascia <BR>84 Indy,86,87SE, and the GT had this style all fascias or inter-changeable so many cars/year my be changed.<BR>The Fiero Store on-line catalog has pics and years, go to Fascias/Bumpers:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.secureleadercom.com/fierostore/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.secureleadercom.com/fierostore/</A> <p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 04-30-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||05-01-2000||12:23 AM||||Z must have a 1988 model from the way he's describing his Fiero's nose. My favorite is the aero nose too. I keep looking at my dead 87 SE, which is the same exact color as my Batmobile, and wondering if I should switch front facias. Probably not, now that I have a new air dam for the pointy nose batty car.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||05-01-2000||09:15 AM||||DAD--They don't all interchange.  The '84 Indy, '85GT and '86SE (maybe '87SE?) had the grooved moulding.  The others had the round style.  I don't think it's removable although I've never actually checked.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||05-01-2000||10:36 AM||||Yes Monkey, Your right, Only the moulding was different, but as far as the fascias they will fit/mount on any year Fiero. I think the mouldings can also be changed??||||reg||11
Z||000005||WKDFIRO||05-01-2000||02:30 PM||||They are all interchangeable. I have the 87-88 Formula nose and rear on my 85 GT. The difference is the "eggcrate" bumper under neath. Basicly if you are able to get everything down to the bumper beam, (Some of the bumper beams had different holes drilled in them, not a big deal but if you can get the beam too it would be that much easier.) However not all are the same trim. The GTs and the 87-88 black strips are smooth where previous have grooves in them.<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 05-01-2000).]||||reg||6
